WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.767
-Thank you, thank you,
thank you, thank you, thank you,

00:00:02.767 --> 00:00:03.968
thank you, thank you.
Enjoy yourself, everybody.

00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:06.834
Welcome, welcome,
welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:06.834 --> 00:00:08.400
You're here. You made it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:11.300
Thank you for watching at home.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:13.400
Well, guys, last night
here on NBC

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:16.300
was the third Republican
presidential debate,

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:19.267
and it's being described
as "unhinged."

00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:21.267
[ Laughter ]

00:00:21.267 --> 00:00:22.334
Oh, yeah.

00:00:22.334 --> 00:00:24.634
There was name-calling,
wild rants,

00:00:24.634 --> 00:00:26.934
and personal attacks.

00:00:26.934 --> 00:00:29.567
Even Trump was watching
like, "Game recognizes game."

00:00:29.567 --> 00:00:33.767
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:35.701
"Game recognize game!"

00:00:35.701 --> 00:00:37.000
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.400
Yeah, it was vicious.
At one point,

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.067
Lester Holt was like,
"We interrupt this debate

00:00:40.067 --> 00:00:42.534
with a 'Real Housewives' reunion
already in progress."

00:00:42.534 --> 00:00:45.033
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:47.100
It was quite a night.
During the two-hour debate,

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.200
Nikki Haley got
the most questions,

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.100
Tim Scott spoke the longest,

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:53.767
and Ron DeSantis spoke
the [coughs] shortest.

00:00:53.767 --> 00:00:55.734
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.734 --> 00:00:57.634
Yeah, one of the big moments
from the night

00:00:57.634 --> 00:01:01.067
was when Vivek Ramaswamy went
after Nikki Haley's daughter

00:01:01.067 --> 00:01:03.400
for being on TikTok.
Watch this.

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:04.801
-I want to laugh
at why Nikki Haley

00:01:04.801 --> 00:01:06.033
didn't answer your question,

00:01:06.033 --> 00:01:07.868
which is about looking
at families in the eye.

00:01:07.868 --> 00:01:09.334
In the last debate,
she made fun of me

00:01:09.334 --> 00:01:12.100
for actually joining TikTok
while her own daughter

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.901
was actually using the app
for a long time.

00:01:13.901 --> 00:01:15.601
So you might want to take care
of your family first.

00:01:15.601 --> 00:01:17.467
-Leave my daughter out
of your voice.

00:01:17.467 --> 00:01:18.701
-Adult daughter.

00:01:18.701 --> 00:01:21.901
The next generation
of Americans are using it.

00:01:21.901 --> 00:01:23.133
Here's the truth.
-You're just scum.

00:01:23.133 --> 00:01:24.334
-The easy answer...

00:01:24.334 --> 00:01:27.300
[ Audience "Oohs" ]
-Ooh.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.000
-Then the moderator tried
to calm things down,

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:30.934
and he was like,
"Nikki, Vivek, remember,

00:01:30.934 --> 00:01:32.634
none of you
are going to be president."

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:34.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.701 --> 00:01:37.234
"Just want to --
Just calm it down."

00:01:37.234 --> 00:01:40.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
"Calm down."

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.067
Not only did the attack
backfire for Vivek,

00:01:42.067 --> 00:01:43.968
it also went viral on TikTok.

00:01:43.968 --> 00:01:46.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:47.801
And get this.
For a while now,

00:01:47.801 --> 00:01:50.100
Tim Scott has claimed
to have a girlfriend,

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:52.434
but no one has ever seen her,

00:01:52.434 --> 00:01:54.901
and donors have been worried
it's hurting him in the race.

00:01:54.901 --> 00:01:58.267
So, after the debate,
he brought her up on stage.

00:01:58.267 --> 00:02:00.267
Yeah. When asked how they met,
she was like,

00:02:00.267 --> 00:02:02.033
"I was his Uber driver
on the way over here."

00:02:02.033 --> 00:02:06.033
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.033 --> 00:02:07.501
Smart move by Tim Scott.

00:02:07.501 --> 00:02:08.801
He's probably not
gonna be president,

00:02:08.801 --> 00:02:10.667
but at least people know
that he has a fake girlfriend.

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:11.901
So that's good.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.901 --> 00:02:13.868
"She lives in Canada.
You guys don't know her."

00:02:13.868 --> 00:02:15.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.133 --> 00:02:16.767
"She doesn't go to school here."

00:02:16.767 --> 00:02:18.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:20.701
Meanwhile, former president
Trump didn't attend the debate

00:02:20.701 --> 00:02:23.901
and said held his own rally
just a few miles away.

00:02:23.901 --> 00:02:25.300
It was the first time
a Trump rally

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:28.534
was the less chaotic
Republican event.

00:02:28.534 --> 00:02:30.033
During the rally,
Trump said Republicans

00:02:30.033 --> 00:02:33.000
should stop wasting time
on debates.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.133
Then he said, "And let's also
stop wasting time on elections

00:02:35.133 --> 00:02:36.534
and just declare me
the winner, okay?

00:02:36.534 --> 00:02:38.000
Come on."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:40.434
Switching gears, you guys,
here's some great news.

00:02:40.434 --> 00:02:43.467
After 118 days,
the Screen Actors Guild

00:02:43.467 --> 00:02:46.067
reached a deal with
the Hollywood studios.

00:02:46.067 --> 00:02:49.400
The strike is over!

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:51.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:51.767 --> 00:02:55.834
-So, tune in tomorrow
when my guests will be everyone.

00:02:55.834 --> 00:02:57.868
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.868 --> 00:02:59.767
Uh, yes, interesting that the --

00:02:59.767 --> 00:03:00.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:00.968 --> 00:03:02.000
♪♪

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.934
Oh, my gosh.
Whoa.

00:03:04.934 --> 00:03:06.734
The guys from
Please Don't Destroy.

00:03:06.734 --> 00:03:09.000
Oh, my gosh.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:12.601
Welcome.
What are you guys doing here?

00:03:12.601 --> 00:03:13.901
Shouldn't you be up at "SNL"?

00:03:13.901 --> 00:03:15.400
-Dude, I'll tell you
what we're doing here.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:16.567
-What?
-We were on the show

00:03:16.567 --> 00:03:17.701
three days ago,
and we couldn't talk about

00:03:17.701 --> 00:03:19.834
our movie
'cause of the actors strike.

00:03:19.834 --> 00:03:22.000
-Yeah, but now it's over,
and we can talk about it.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:24.067
So why don't you book us?

00:03:24.067 --> 00:03:25.267
-What do you mean,
why don't we book you?

00:03:25.267 --> 00:03:26.667
You were just here.

00:03:26.667 --> 00:03:28.901
-Yeah, but we weren't able
to talk about our movie.

00:03:28.901 --> 00:03:31.567
"Please Don't Destroy:
The Treasure of Foggy Mountain,"

00:03:31.567 --> 00:03:33.701
coming out on Peacock.
-Yeah, well...

00:03:33.701 --> 00:03:36.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:36.734 --> 00:03:39.901
Well, you come back,
and you can talk about it.

00:03:39.901 --> 00:03:42.434
-Who do you have booked tonight?
-We're fully booked.

00:03:42.434 --> 00:03:43.801
We have Jared Leto
on the show tonight.

00:03:43.801 --> 00:03:47.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:47.267 --> 00:03:49.434
-Well, what movie
does he have coming out?

00:03:49.434 --> 00:03:50.834
-He's not talking
about a movie.

00:03:50.834 --> 00:03:53.467
He's announcing a world tour
with Thirty Seconds to Mars.

00:03:53.467 --> 00:03:54.834
-So he's not talking about

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:55.901
"Please Don't Destroy:
The Treasure of Foggy Mountain,"

00:03:55.901 --> 00:03:57.968
coming out
November 17th on Peacock?

00:03:57.968 --> 00:03:59.501
-No, he's not talking about it.

00:03:59.501 --> 00:04:02.701
-Oh, okay.
-Okay. Who else is on the show?

00:04:02.701 --> 00:04:04.901
-AJR is on the show tonight.

00:04:04.901 --> 00:04:06.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:06.234 --> 00:04:08.267
-Oh.

00:04:08.267 --> 00:04:10.033
So AJR is going to talk about

00:04:10.033 --> 00:04:12.734
"Please Don't Destroy:
The Treasure of Foggy Mountain,"

00:04:12.734 --> 00:04:15.601
coming out on peacock.com

00:04:15.601 --> 00:04:17.934
November 17th?
You can sign up today.

00:04:17.934 --> 00:04:21.467
-Uh, no, AJR is not going to
talk about that at all.

00:04:21.467 --> 00:04:23.234
They're a great band,
and they have a new album

00:04:23.234 --> 00:04:24.934
coming out tonight --
at midnight, actually.

00:04:24.934 --> 00:04:26.400
Tonight. Yeah.
-Wow. So then...

00:04:26.400 --> 00:04:29.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:29.167 --> 00:04:30.534
I mean, I just don't understand

00:04:30.534 --> 00:04:32.834
how the hell anyone
is going to find out about

00:04:32.834 --> 00:04:35.501
"Please Don't Destroy:
The Treasure of Foggy Mountain,"

00:04:35.501 --> 00:04:38.100
which is coming out, uh,
November 17th on Peacock.

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:40.567
[ Laughter ]

00:04:40.567 --> 00:04:42.200
-Yeah, I don't know
how that's going to happen.

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:44.334
I'm sorry.
I'm sorry to let you down.

00:04:44.334 --> 00:04:47.133
-Okay. Alright. We're gonna
go do "Seth." Um...

00:04:47.133 --> 00:04:49.400
-Wow.
-Before --

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:50.834
Before we leave,
we just want to say

00:04:50.834 --> 00:04:54.133
this audience is
the best audience in the world!

00:04:54.133 --> 00:04:56.501
-Get out of here!

00:04:56.501 --> 00:04:58.300
-Love you, Jimmy.

00:04:58.300 --> 00:04:59.434
-Bye, guys.

00:04:59.434 --> 00:05:00.834
Get out of here!

00:05:00.834 --> 00:05:03.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:03.133 --> 00:05:07.334
Get out of here!
Please Don't Destroy!

00:05:07.334 --> 00:05:08.701
Please Don't Destroy.

00:05:08.701 --> 00:05:10.467
No one's gonna talk
about it.

00:05:10.467 --> 00:05:11.767
The strike is...

00:05:11.767 --> 00:05:14.133
[ Laughs ]

00:05:14.133 --> 00:05:17.200
That's just so funny.

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:20.167
Guys, anyway, as I was saying,
the strike is finally over.

00:05:20.167 --> 00:05:22.868
That's right. When the actors
heard a deal had been reached,

00:05:22.868 --> 00:05:24.801
they gasped, screamed,
laughed, cried,

00:05:24.801 --> 00:05:26.901
and then were like,
"I also do accents."

00:05:26.901 --> 00:05:28.334
[ Laughter ]

00:05:28.334 --> 00:05:30.467
Seriously, the actors are back
just in time.

00:05:30.467 --> 00:05:32.434
I'm not sure the world
could handle another reality

00:05:32.434 --> 00:05:33.901
dating show.
Am I right?

00:05:33.901 --> 00:05:36.400
[ Laughter, audience groans ]

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:38.901
Speaking of --
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.901 --> 00:05:40.501
Like, you recognize
maybe two of those.

00:05:40.501 --> 00:05:41.868
Come on.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.868 --> 00:05:44.234
Speaking of, tonight was the
"Women Tell All" episode

00:05:44.234 --> 00:05:46.167
of "The Golden Bachelor."

00:05:46.167 --> 00:05:47.234
-Ooh.
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:05:47.234 --> 00:05:48.434
-Yeah.
'Cause who doesn't love

00:05:48.434 --> 00:05:50.000
hearing their grandma
describe sex?

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:51.567
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.567 --> 00:05:53.534
-Oy!
-"You pulled the muscle

00:05:53.534 --> 00:05:54.601
in the fantasy suite?

00:05:54.601 --> 00:05:56.400
I pulled a muscle
in the fantasy suite."

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:58.901
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.901 --> 00:06:00.834
You guys see this?
Starting next month,

00:06:00.834 --> 00:06:04.667
Disney+ and Hulu are going
to be merged into the same app.

00:06:04.667 --> 00:06:06.701
-Ooh.
-Yep, streamers are merging.

00:06:06.701 --> 00:06:08.400
Pretty soon, they're
gonna be all in one

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:10.000
giant app called cable.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:12.734
[ Laughter ]

00:06:12.734 --> 00:06:14.834
What are we doing?
What are we doing?

00:06:14.834 --> 00:06:16.167
[ Applause ]

00:06:16.167 --> 00:06:19.200
What have we done?
-Come on.

00:06:19.200 --> 00:06:21.701
-Yep. Disney+ and Hulu
are merging into one app.

00:06:21.701 --> 00:06:23.234
That's good.
Now, when your kid tries

00:06:23.234 --> 00:06:26.067
to turn on "Bluey," he'll wind
up bingeing "Sons of Anarchy."

00:06:26.067 --> 00:06:28.400
[ Laughter ]

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:29.701
Hey, it's good to see you, bud.

00:06:29.701 --> 00:06:31.067
I feel like we haven't
caught up in a while.

00:06:31.067 --> 00:06:32.534
-Oh, wow.
I'm good.

00:06:32.534 --> 00:06:33.934
Thanks for checking in, buddy.

00:06:33.934 --> 00:06:36.000
-[ Chuckles ]
What have you been up to lately?

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.834
-Not much.
Well, I was in Grand Rapids

00:06:37.834 --> 00:06:40.133
the other day.
-Oh. How was that?

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:42.000
Good. Had a little trouble
getting an Uber,

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:43.400
but I figured it out.

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:45.234
-In Grand Rapids
over the weekend,

00:06:45.234 --> 00:06:48.567
an Amazon truck was stolen
and then taken on a joy ride.

00:06:48.567 --> 00:06:52.200
[ Laughter ]

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:53.801
-What else have
you been up to?

00:06:53.801 --> 00:06:55.501
-You know, lots of travel.

00:06:55.501 --> 00:06:58.501
Check out this small town
called McKees Rocks.

00:06:58.501 --> 00:07:00.200
Just watch cars go by.
It was great.

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:02.400
-Police in McKees Rocks
arrested a man they say

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:05.334
was trying to expose himself
to passing drivers.

00:07:05.334 --> 00:07:09.234
[ Laughter ]

00:07:09.234 --> 00:07:11.267
-Sounds like you've been busy.
Anything else?

00:07:11.267 --> 00:07:12.834
-Let me think.
Um...

00:07:12.834 --> 00:07:14.434
Oh, I went to my house
in Connecticut,

00:07:14.434 --> 00:07:16.868
just west of Hartford.
Did some gardening -- Oh.

00:07:16.868 --> 00:07:18.634
So relaxing.
-In Burlington, Connecticut,

00:07:18.634 --> 00:07:20.501
west of Hartford,
a man is now charged

00:07:20.501 --> 00:07:22.367
with running
an illegal psychedelic mushroom

00:07:22.367 --> 00:07:24.367
growing operation
out of a house.

00:07:24.367 --> 00:07:26.100
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:28.334
-Wow. You've had a lot
on your plate.

00:07:28.334 --> 00:07:30.634
-Yeah. Also, I went down
to my winter place.

00:07:30.634 --> 00:07:32.634
The Villages in Florida.
You know me.

00:07:32.634 --> 00:07:34.501
Work hard, play hard.

00:07:34.501 --> 00:07:36.534
-A man who lives
in The Villages

00:07:36.534 --> 00:07:38.000
was arrested by the feds,

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:41.567
accused of having thousands of
dollars worth of illegal pills

00:07:41.567 --> 00:07:43.868
used to treat
erectile dysfunction.

00:07:43.868 --> 00:07:45.100
[ Laughter ]

00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:48.501
-Well, it was nice
catching up with you.

00:07:48.501 --> 00:07:50.400
-Hang on.
I'm on the phone with my doctor.

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:53.234
Yeah, well, it's been way
longer than four hours.

00:07:53.234 --> 00:07:54.634
-All right, Steve Higgins,
everybody.

00:07:54.634 --> 00:07:55.767
Steve.

00:07:55.767 --> 00:08:01.267
[ Applause ]

00:08:01.267 --> 00:08:03.400
Guys, I heard about
two women in Michigan

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:06.200
who are accused
of embezzling $20,000

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:07.834
from a Girl Scout troop.

00:08:07.834 --> 00:08:09.834
-Oh.
-$20,000.

00:08:09.834 --> 00:08:11.767
That's almost the amount
your co-worker guilts you

00:08:11.767 --> 00:08:14.267
into buying each year.
[ Laughter ]

00:08:14.267 --> 00:08:16.234
Apparently, one of the women
accused was like, "She did it.

00:08:16.234 --> 00:08:17.734
I was just a tagalong."

00:08:17.734 --> 00:08:19.501
[ Laughter ]

00:08:19.501 --> 00:08:20.734
-Come on!

00:08:20.734 --> 00:08:29.901
♪♪

00:08:29.901 --> 00:08:33.100
-Guys, listen to this.
A U.S.-bound flight from London

00:08:33.100 --> 00:08:35.734
had to turn around
after crew members realized

00:08:35.734 --> 00:08:38.334
that the plane
was missing two windows.

00:08:38.334 --> 00:08:41.067
[ Laughter ]

00:08:41.067 --> 00:08:42.601
Then they landed
and we were like, "Oh, crap.

00:08:42.601 --> 00:08:44.200
We're also missing
two passengers."

00:08:44.200 --> 00:08:45.300
[ Laughter ]

